{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTranspositionExpansion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTranspositionExpansion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_all","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L555-L560","doc":"**`HeckeJucysMurphyReduction`'s residual hypothesis, discharged.**  That file reduced full\ncommutativity to the adjacent pairs and stated the remainder as an assumption; `jmRaw_comm_adjacent`\nsupplies it, so the reduction now stands unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L550-L553","doc":"**The adjacent case**, `[L_k, L_{k+1}] = 0` — the one case `HeckeJucysMurphyReduction` could not\nclose, and the reason its `jmRaw_comm_all_of_all_adjacent` had to take a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm","kind":"theorem","line":535,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L535-L548","doc":"**The multiplicative Jucys–Murphy elements commute.**\n\n`L_i L_k = L_k L_i` for all `i, k`, unconditionally.  Expanding both as `1 + A`, the cross terms are\n`A_i + A_k` on each side and the quadratic term is `addJM_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_eq_one_add_addJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_eq_one_add_addJM","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L522-L533","doc":"**The two families coincide up to a shift**: `L_k = 1 + A_k` at `d = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_comm","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L494-L503","doc":"**The additive Jucys–Murphy elements commute** — for every `d`, and with no hypothesis on `q`\nbeyond `H`'s own relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_comm_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_comm_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L481-L492","doc":"**The telescoping step**: `A_i` commutes with `A_{m+1}` whenever `i ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSum_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSum_succ","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L477-L479","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_addJM_of_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_addJM_of_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L456-L464","doc":"The same lift for `A_i` itself, via the expansion `A_i = d · Σ_{l<i} T_(l,i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_transp_of_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_transp_of_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L429-L454","doc":"If `X` commutes with every generator `σ_j` for `j < i`, it commutes with `T_(l,i)` — every\nletter of that word has index in `[l, i−1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum_ne","kind":"theorem","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L407-L417","doc":"**Jucys's centrality property**: `σ_j` commutes with `S_m` for every `j ≠ m`.\n\nThis is the statement the measurement found, now proved.  It is the input to the telescoping\nargument `A_m = S_m − S_{m−1}`, which yields commutativity **without ever using** the product half\nof 3.24(iii) — the step that `HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.addJM_sigma_prod_swap` showed is entangled\nwith the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum_above","kind":"theorem","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L396-L405","doc":"**Centrality above the cutoff**: for `j > m`, `σ_j` commutes with `S_m` — every index in the sum\nis below `j`, so `sigma_comm_addJM_small` applies term by term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSum","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L370-L394","doc":"**Centrality below the cutoff**: for `j < m`, `σ_j` commutes with `S_m`.\n\nSplit `range (m+1)` into `{j, j+1}` and the rest.  The pair is `addJM_sigma_comm_add`; each other\nindex is `sigma_comm_addJM_small` (below `j`) or `sigma_comm_addJM` (above `j+1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSum","kind":"def","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L366-L368","doc":"Partial sum `S_m = Σ_{i ≤ m} A_i` (the `i = 0` term is `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJM_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJM_small","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L346-L354","doc":"**3.24(i), the easy direction**: `σ_j` commutes with `A_i` when `i < j`.  Every letter of every\n`T_(l,i)` has index `≤ i−1 ≤ j−2`, so `sigma_comm_transp_far` applies term by term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJM","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L310-L344","doc":"**Mathas 3.24(i)** (the `i > j+1` case): `σ_j` commutes with `A_i`.\n\nAssembled from the three commutation lemmas by splitting `Σ_{l<i} T_(l,i)` on `l`:\n\n| `l` | lemma | ingredient |\n|---|---|---|\n| `l < j` | `sigma_comm_transp_disjoint` | braid |\n| `l ∈ {j, j+1}` | `sigma_comm_transp_pair` — **as a pair** | braid + Hecke |\n| `l > j+1` | `sigma_comm_transp_below` | braid |\n\nThe middle row is the one that cannot be done term-by-term: neither `T_(j,i)` nor `T_(j+1,i)`\ncommutes with `σ_j` alone (measured), only their sum does.  That is why the expansion into a **sum**\nwas the necessary ingredient rather than a convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_below","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L282-L306","doc":"`σ_j` commutes with `T_(l,i)` when `j + 1 < l` — every letter of `T_(l,i)` has index in\n`[l, i−1]`, all at distance `≥ 2` above `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L254-L280","doc":"**Disjoint transpositions commute**: `σ_j` commutes with `T_(l,i)` for `l < j` and `i > j+1`.\n\nInduction on `i` above the base case `i = j+2`: each step conjugates by `σ_{i−1}` with\n`i−1 > j+1`, which `σ_j` commutes past by far-commutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_base","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L224-L252","doc":"**The hard base case**: `σ_j` commutes with `T_(l,j+2)` for `l < j`.\n\n`T_(l,j+2) = v u X u v` with `u = σ_j`, `v = σ_{j+1}` and `X = T_(l,j)`, and `X` commutes with `v`\nby `sigma_comm_transp_far` (every letter of `X` has index `≤ j−1`).  Then two braid moves close it:\n\n    u · v u X u v = (uvu) X u v = (vuv) X u v = v u X (vuv) = v u X (uvu) = v u X u v · u\n\nOnly the braid relation is used — no Hecke relation here, in contrast to the pair-swap law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_far","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L196-L222","doc":"`σ_m` commutes with `T_(l,i)` when `m > i` — every letter of `T_(l,i)` has index `≤ i−1`, so all\nare at distance `≥ 2` from `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_transp_pair","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L118-L185","doc":"**Pair-swap law**: for `i > j+1`, `σ_j` commutes with `T_(j,i) + T_(j+1,i)`.\n\nBase case `i = j+2`, with `u = σ_j`, `v = σ_{j+1}`: the claim is `u(vuv + v) = (vuv + v)u`.  One\nbraid move turns `uvu` into `vuv` on each side, leaving `vuv² + uv = v²uv + vu`, and the **Hecke\nrelation** `v² = hv + 1` expands both to `h·vuv + uv + vu`.  Braid alone is not enough — the Hecke\nrelation is what makes the leftover terms cancel.\n\nStep `i → i+1`: both transpositions gain the same outer conjugation by `σ_i`, and `σ_j` commutes\nwith `σ_i` because `i > j+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_eq_transp_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_eq_transp_sum","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L81-L106","doc":"**The sum-of-transpositions expansion**: `A_k = d · Σ_{i<k} T_(i,k)`.\n\nInduction on `k`.  The step is exactly the recursion: conjugating each `T_(i,k)` by `σ_k` produces\n`T_(i,k+1)`, and the extra `d·σ_k` supplies the new top term `T_(k,k+1)`.\n\nNote the **uniform** coefficient `d` — a consequence of this corpus's recursion\n`A_{k+1} = σ_k A_k σ_k + d·σ_k`, which places `d` on the new term only.  Mathas's recursion places\n`q⁻¹` outside both terms and yields geometric coefficients instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_pred","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L77-L79","doc":"`T_(k−1,k) = σ_{k−1}` — the adjacent transposition is the generator itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_succ","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L73-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp_self","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L69-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.transp","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean#L63-L67","doc":"**The transposition element `T_(i,k)`**, defined as a conjugate of a generator — no new axioms.\n`T_(k,k+1) = σ_k`, and `T_(i,k+1) = σ_k T_(i,k) σ_k` for `i < k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}